      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Fix language picker localization",
        "body": "## Summary\n- Render each language picker option in its own stable/native language, with System and English shown in English.\n- Cache localized bundle lookups per language so picker rendering does not repeat filesystem bundle resolution.\n- Stop writing explicit app language choices into `AppleLanguages`, and clear stale app-level overrides so System follows macOS language preferences again.\n\n## Why\nUsers can accidentally choose a language they do not understand. The language picker must remain readable enough for them to recover, regardless of the current app language. System should also mean the actual macOS-preferred language, not the last explicit CodexBar language selection.\n\nRoot cause: explicit language choices were being mirrored into `AppleLanguages`, which could cause System mode to inherit the previous app override. The picker label lookup also bypassed the existing bundle cache when resolving per-language labels.\n\n## Validation\n- `swift test --filter 'PreferencesPaneSmokeTests|LocalizationBundleCacheTests|LocalizationLanguageCatalogTests'`\n- `make check`\n- `make test` across all 46 shards\n- Covered the Korean -> System regression with a defaults test that seeds a stale `AppleLanguages` override and verifies it is cleared.",
